WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:12.799
Hi! Have you ever been in a situation where
you couldn’t remember the word you wanted?

00:00:12.799 --> 00:00:18.550
Don’t worry! It happens to everyone, even
native speakers! And in a speaking exam, when

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:24.090
you’re maybe nervous and stressed, it can
be even worse! So here are four things you

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:29.160
can do to communicate when you don’t know
or can’t remember a word in English.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:38.100
The first technique is to find a more general
word or explain the word. For example, if

00:00:38.101 --> 00:00:43.370
you can’t remember the word ‘surgeon’,
you could say ‘doctor’ or if you can’t

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:47.960
remember the word ‘kitten’, you could
say ‘baby cat’.

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:52.880
Describing the purpose

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:57.969
of an item in a sentence can also be useful.
If you don’t know the word ‘scissors’,

00:00:57.969 --> 00:01:02.659
you could say ‘They are used to cut paper’
or ‘They’re used for cutting paper’.

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:05.280
This works best for nouns.

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:14.870
For nouns and adjectives,
you can use synonyms. Synonyms are simply

00:01:14.870 --> 00:01:20.350
two words that mean the same or have a very similar meaning. For example, ‘clever’

00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:27.090
is a synonym for ‘intelligent’, and ‘stone’
is a synonym for ‘rock’. Antonyms are

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:31.900
opposite words. You can often describe an
adjective using the opposite adjective. If

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:40.950
you can’t remember the word ‘old’ you
could say ‘not young’, for example.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:46.549
One more technique to use when you can’t remember
a word is approximations. You can say ‘it’s

00:01:46.549 --> 00:01:50.420
like a house’ or ‘it’s a kind of house
with only one floor’ when you’re trying

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:56.030
to describe a bungalow. Remember you can always
use more than one of these language techniques

00:01:56.030 --> 00:02:01.229
at once. So if you can’t remember the word
for ‘office block’, you could say ‘it’s

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:05.600
a kind of tall building where people go to
work at desks’.

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:21.440
For more tips on learning

00:02:21.519 --> 00:02:25.530
English and preparing for your exam, subscribe
to our channel and visit the LearnEnglish

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:29.520
Teens website where you will find loads more
learning material to help you improve your

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:31.040
English!

